  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 218 PM MST FRI NOV 6 2026\nThe area will continue to sit under broad west-southwest flow \nMonday through midweek. On Monday, a weak Pacific shortwave \ntrough will pass over north-central ID, bringing small chances \nof precipitation over the northernmost mountains of our CWA late\nMonday into early Tuesday. Otherwise, a highly amplified \nPacific ridge will build into the western CONUS Tuesday through \nThursday, continuing dry conditions and temperatures 10 to 15 \ndegrees above normal. Come Friday, there is general guidance \nagreement of an incoming upper low from the Gulf of Alaska \ndigging into the Pacific northwest region, keeping our area \nunder a strong southwest flow. There is considerable uncertainty\nover the arrival of precipitation over our area. For now, \nFriday will see slight chances of rain and mountain snow and the\nbeginning of a slight cooldown.",
